"mobile_phone","la":14.605009,"lo":-61.072721,"d":292},{"n":"St. Louis Cathedral, Fort-de-France","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":14.604167,"lo":-61.07,"d":92,"ds":"St. Louis Cathedral (French: Cathédrale Saint-Louis de Fort-de-France) is a Catholic cathedral in Martinique, an overseas department of France. It was built in the late 19th-century in the Romanesque Revival style and serves as the cathedral of the Roman Catholic Archdiocese of Fort-de-France.","wpu":"St. Louis Cathedral, Fort-de-France","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Cath%C3%A9drale_Saint_Louis.jpg/960px-Cath%C3%A9drale_Saint_Louis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Arrondissement of Fort-de-France","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":14.607778,"lo":-61.071944,"d":373,"ds":"The arrondissement of Fort-de-France (French: arrondissement de Fort-de-France) is an arrondissement in the French overseas region and department of Martinique. It has four communes. Its population is 150,038 (2021), and its area is 171.0 km2 (66.0 sq mi).","wpu":"Arrondissement of Fort-de-France","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Locator_map_of_Arrondissement_Fort-de-France_2018.png/960px-Locator_map_of_Arrondissement_Fort-de-France_2018.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Communauté d'agglomération du Centre de la Martinique","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":14.61,"lo":-61.07,"d":555,"ds":"Communauté d'agglomération du Centre de la Martinique is the communauté d'agglomération, an intercommunal structure, centred on the city of Fort-de-France. It is located in Martinique, an overseas department and region of France. It was created in January 2001.","wpu":"Communauté d'agglomération du Centre de la Martinique","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Localisation_CA_du_Centre_de_la_Martinique.svg/960px-Localisation_CA_du_Centre_de_la_Martinique.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Parc naturel régional de la Martinique","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":14.611111,"lo":-61.084167,"d":1668,"ds":"Parc naturel régional de la Martinique (French pronunciation: [paʁk natyʁɛl ʁeʒjɔnal də la maʁtinik]) is one of 54 French regional nature parks. With a surface area of approximately 63,000 ha (240 sq mi), it covers more than half of the island, overlapping 32 of 34 communes – including approximately 100,000 inhabitants. The park works to preserve one of 34 biodiversity hotspots on the planet.","wpu":"Parc naturel régional de la Martinique","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/La_cascade_de_Didier_Parc_Naturel_R%C3%A9gional_de_Martinique.jpg/960px-La_cascade_de_Didier_Parc_Naturel_R%C3%A9gional_de_Martinique.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Fort-de-France Bay","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":14.566667,"lo":-61.05,"d":4775,"ds":"Fort-de-France Bay is a large inlet of the Caribbean Sea, off the coast of Martinique. It is named after Martinique's capital, Fort-de-France, located north of the bay.","wpu":"Fort-de-France Bay","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Vent%C3%B4se_Fort-de-France_IMG_20201011_114043.jpg/960px-Vent%C3%B4se_Fort-de-France_IMG_20201011_114043.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Martinique","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":14.65,"lo":-61.015,"d":7749,"ds":"Martinique ( MAR-tin-EEK, French pronunciation: [maʁtinik] ; Martinican Creole: Matinik or Matnik; Kalinago: Madinina or Madiana) is an island in the Lesser Antilles of the West Indies, in the eastern Caribbean Sea. A part of the French West Indies (Antilles), Martinique is an overseas department and region and a single territorial collectivity of France.","wpu":"Martinique","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Martinique-de-haut_%28cropped%29.jpg/960px-Martinique-de-haut_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Saint-Joseph, Martinique","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":14.6708,"lo":-61.0375,"d":8109,"ds":"Saint-Joseph (French pronunciation: [sɛ̃ ʒozɛf]) is a commune in the Arrondissement of Fort-de-France on Martinique.","wpu":"Saint-Joseph, Martinique","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Locator_map_of_Saint-Joseph_-_Martinique_2018.png/960px-Locator_map_of_Saint-Joseph_-_Martinique_2018.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Fort-de-France (, US also , French: [fɔʁ də fʁɑ̃s] ; Martinican Creole: Fodfwans) is a commune and the capital city of Martinique, an overseas department and region of France located in the Caribbean.","wpu":"Fort-de-France","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Fort-de-france-harbor.jpg/960px-Fort-de-france-harbor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}